  "note": "Municipal elections, 21 May 1952: two councillors for each of the six wards; there was no election for aldermen, who held office until 1955. Sixteen nominations were received for the twelve seats; North Ward was the only contest after withdrawals in West Ward (Larne Times, 8, 22 and 29 May 1952). No party labels are printed for the unopposed members. Image-read (meetings corroboration, 7 Nov 2026): Barstow 514, not 614; the second winner is printed 'Charles Locton' in the News-Letter result and 'Charles Lockton' in the nominations and the Irish News, which prints his vote as 486 against the News-Letter's 481."
